Z||000000||Fiero_24||10-19-2001||08:25 AM||||I have always wanted to take these scoops from and older trans am:<BR> <A HREF="http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/ebayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=596901484&r=0&t=0" TARGET=_blank>http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/ebayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=596901484&r=0&t=0</A> <P>and use them as 1/4 panel scoops on a Fiero.  Just wondering if anyone has tried them or not.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/driverside41.jpg"> <BR>  <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||10-19-2001||08:55 AM||||There is a guy in the NIFE club who is having them installed as side scoops on his 87 Blue GT. He was trying to have the panels done by Fierorama but wasn't able to get them completed by then. You'll probably see them in the spring.<BR><P>------------------<BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">          <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><B><I>Happiness isn't around the corner...<BR>Happiness IS the corner.</I></B></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Sage||10-19-2001||09:19 AM||||My son picked up a set of those at a swap meet in Columbus for $10.00 last summer.  We grafted them into his hood as cooling- pressure relief vents.  Looks and works pretty good, except for the paint "bubble" that developed about a month later!(water in the air lines is my guess)  We are going to repaint the hood after he gets the V6 swap done.  I think they would work and look super as 1/4 panel scoops.  Get 'em and just do it!<P>------------------<BR>Have a good one!||||reg||1
