Z||000010||Fiero_24||10-19-2001||01:54 PM||||Reality those look really good!  If I don't use them on the 1/4 panels, I may put them on the hood.<BR><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/driverside41.jpg"> <BR>  <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||1
Z||000011||Reality||10-19-2001||03:33 PM||||Thanks for all the praise. It wasn't that hard but then again I had a good teacher.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> Since the hood is already in two layers you just carefully cut the top layer to accept the scoop, and the bottom layer, make the opening a bit smaller so the scoop sits on it. I think I had to wedge mine until I got some glass in place, then it's just a matter of time and well more time. Can't say enough how grateful I was to Sage for helping put these in. (Was one of my first attempts at fiberglass and major body work) And besides the major bubble that now sits between the scoops they are an awesome sight. (Just had to get you on that one Dad) I did forget to measure where they were going to land on the backside, and ended up haveing to shave a bit, but it was for the better. There are I think four bolts per scoop that sit in platforms that we took out then sanded the platform smooth. Also had to change my fan out to a differnt year I think an 86, for some reason my 88 fan shroud had these little ridges on it that kept hitting the scoop, so out it came and the smooth one went in. OK I rambled enough enjoy!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Reality<p>[This message has been edited by Reality (edited 10-19-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000012||Jncomutt||10-19-2001||05:16 PM||||Those are the first Nice hood vents I've seen.  I wasn't really too much a fan of the other ones 'i've seen' people using but those are sweet!  If I only knew the slightest bit about body work....||||reg||1
